  "dom_id": "step-q132712",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "In a factory, the amount of sugar on a cookie is normally distributed with a mean of $15$ grams and a standard deviation of $0.8$ grams. What is the probability that the amount of sugar on a randomly selected cookie is less than $14$ grams? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1093\\,$ | $\\,0.1075\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1292\\,$ | $\\,0.1271\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1515\\,$ | $\\,0.1492\\,$ | $\\,0.1469\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the amount of sugar (in grams) on the cookies. Then we have $X\u223cN(15,{0.8}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X<14).$ First, we write this as a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\nP(X<14)=P(X\\le 14)\n$$\n\nThen, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 14) & =P(Z\\le \\frac{14-15}{0.8}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.25) \\\\  & =\u03a6(-1.25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-1.25)=0.1056\u22480.11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the amount of sugar on a randomly selected cookie is less than $14$ grams is approximately $0.11.$",
